{{ 'character-page.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'component-price.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'product-card.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<script src="{{ 'ap-character-cuts.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>

{%- style -%}
  .section-{{ section.id }}-padding {
    padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top | times: 0.75 | round: 0 }}px;
    padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom | times: 0.75 | round: 0 }}px;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .section-{{ section.id }}-padding {
      padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px;
      padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px;
    }
  }
{%- endstyle -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Alterpop — Character grid. Source of truth: Wireframe 9a (Character Page).
  Renders on templates/metaobject/character.json, alongside character-header.

  Data source: metaobject.products.value — a list.product_reference field,
  confirmed on the live `character` metaobject definition (17/09/2026). Max
  128 references, no native pagination/sort/filters (it's a metaobject field,
  not a Shopify collection) — the whole array renders on one page, same as
  the wireframe's "full grid shows immediately, no filter chosen first."

  Zero products -> the section renders nothing (no empty-state copy, no grid
  markup) per the corrected briefing: "Com zero produtos o template renderiza
  header sem meta line e sem grid."

  DEAD REFERENCES (18/09/2026, measured — not assumed): a reference to a
  product the storefront can't see is NOT delivered as a blank entry. Tested
  with a DRAFT product on a throwaway entry (`qa-dead-ref`, 2 references):
  Shopify drops it from metaobject.products.value before Liquid runs — .size
  and .count both came back 1, and even the un-guarded code rendered 1 card
  and "1 figure". So today ap_visible == .size. The `blank` skips below are a
  safety net for a shape that was NOT observed (a deleted product, or an
  ACTIVE one merely unpublished from the Online Store, were not tested); they
  cost nothing, and without the skip in the second pass a blank would fall
  into `unless product.available` and render an empty card. ap_visible gates
  the wrapper. "No products" rule unchanged: zero visible cards -> nothing
  rendered, no message, no placeholder.

  CARD: reuses snippets/product-card.liquid unmodified (the actual shared
  component — "Product Card standard, sem variante"), plus the existing
  `hide_franchise` param (same reasoning as Universe Room: the page is
  already scoped to one character/universe, so FRANCHISE on every card is
  redundant with the header) and a new opt-in `show_tier` param (added here,
  see snippets/product-card.liquid) for "tier label from COLLECTOR up."

  GRID WRAPPER: intentionally NOT sections/main-collection-product-grid.liquid.
  That section is deeply bound to a Shopify `collection` object — paginate,
  collection.filters, collection.sort_options, <collection-component
  data-collection-id="{{ collection.id }}">. None of that exists for a
  metaobject's product-reference array, so "reusing the Line grid" means
  reusing its two genuinely portable parts instead of the whole section:
  snippets/product-card.liquid (the card) and the sold-out-last two-pass
  sort pattern from main-collection-product-grid.liquid (used there for
  Universe Room). Each grid item is a plain <div class="grid__item"> (not
  Dawn's <li> from snippets/product-card-grid-item.liquid) so it can carry
  the cuts engine's data-line/-height/-year attributes and sit as a direct
  sibling of the cluster-heading <div> that assets/ap-character-cuts.js
  injects when a cut is active — <div> siblings inside a <ul> would be
  invalid list content.

  SORT: available products first, then sold-out (visible, marked, pushed to
  the end), each group keeping the metaobject array's own order — identical
  rule to main-collection-product-grid.liquid's Universe Room pass, just
  over an in-memory array instead of a paginated collection (no paginate.pages
  gate needed: the array is never paginated in the first place).

  CUTS: EXPLORE BY renders all three chips (Line / Height / Year) — the DOM
  contract in assets/ap-character-cuts.js already disables a chip with no
  live data anywhere in the grid (see tests/fixtures/character-grid.html,
  Instance B). Line is wired to product.metafields.alterpop.line (exists on
  the definition, currently null on every sampled product — chip renders
  disabled until the sync app populates it). Height and Year carry NO
  data-height/data-year attribute at all: there is no year field on Product,
  and ociostock.dimensions is a full package L×W×H string, not a single
  comparable height — parsing it to fake a bucket would be inference. Both
  chips are therefore permanently dead today, exactly as the fixture's
  Instance B exercises, and need no separate Liquid-side disabling logic.

  The whole EXPLORE BY bar is server-side gated on ap_any_line (18/09/2026
  briefing): with Height/Year permanently dead and Line currently empty on
  every product, rendering the bar at all would mean a labelled container
  holding three JS-disabled buttons and nothing to explore — worse than no
  bar. `ap-character-cuts.js` only disables per-chip client-side (it can't
  decide "hide the whole bar", and doing that in JS would flash the full bar
  before disabling); Liquid decides visibility here from the same data the
  JS itself reads. NOTE: this check only inspects alterpop.line — the one
  field actually wired to data-* today. If Height or Year is ever wired
  (their own field lands, code starts emitting data-height/data-year), this
  condition needs to grow to match, or the bar will hide even though one of
  those newly-live cuts has data.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign ap_products = metaobject.products.value

  assign ap_visible = 0
  assign ap_any_line = false
  for product in ap_products
    if product == blank
      continue
    endif
    assign ap_visible = ap_visible | plus: 1
    if product.metafields.alterpop.line.value != blank
      assign ap_any_line = true
    endif
  endfor
-%}

{%- if ap_visible > 0 -%}
  <div class="ap-character-grid section-{{ section.id }}-padding page-width">
    {%- if ap_any_line -%}
      <div class="ap-character-cuts" data-ap-cut-bar>
        <span class="ap-character-cuts__label type-label">{{ 'sections.catalogue.explore_by' | t }}</span>
        <button type="button" class="ap-btn ap-btn--chip" data-ap-cut-chip="line" aria-pressed="false">
          {{- 'sections.catalogue.cut_line' | t -}}
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="ap-btn ap-btn--chip" data-ap-cut-chip="height" aria-pressed="false">
          {{- 'sections.catalogue.cut_height' | t -}}
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="ap-btn ap-btn--chip" data-ap-cut-chip="year" aria-pressed="false">
          {{- 'sections.catalogue.cut_year' | t -}}
        </button>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div
      class="grid ap-character-grid__items"
      data-ap-grid
      data-ap-cut-grid
      data-ap-cut=""
      id="CharacterGrid-{{ section.id }}"
    >
      {%- liquid
        assign ap_index = 0
        for product in ap_products
          if product == blank
            continue
          endif
          if product.available
            assign ap_index = ap_index | plus: 1
            assign ap_line = product.metafields.alterpop.line.value | join: ', '
            assign ap_skip_styles = false
            unless ap_index == 1
              assign ap_skip_styles = true
            endunless
            render 'character-grid-item', product: product, index: ap_index, section: section, skip_styles: ap_skip_styles, line: ap_line
          endif
        endfor
        for product in ap_products
          if product == blank
            continue
          endif
          unless product.available
            assign ap_index = ap_index | plus: 1
            assign ap_line = product.metafields.alterpop.line.value | join: ', '
            render 'character-grid-item', product: product, index: ap_index, section: section, skip_styles: true, line: ap_line
          endunless
        endfor
      -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Character grid",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "t:sections.all.padding.padding_top",
      "default": 24
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "t:sections.all.padding.padding_bottom",
      "default": 48
    }
  ],
  "enabled_on": {
    "templates": ["metaobject"]
  }
}
{% endschema %}
